12
00:59:02,399 --> 00:59:08,399
Blade: Trinity is a 2004 American superhero film based
on the Marvel Comics character Blade.

13
01:03:57,599 --> 01:04:03,599
It is the sequel to Blade II (2002) and the third
installment in the Blade franchise.

14
01:08:52,800 --> 01:08:58,800
Written and directed by David S.

15
01:13:48,000 --> 01:13:54,000
Goyer, it stars Wesley Snipes as the title character, alongside Ryan Reynolds, Jessica
Biel, Kris Kristofferson, Dominic Purcell, Parker Posey, and Triple H.

16
01:18:43,199 --> 01:18:49,199
Vampire leader Danica Talos has framed Blade for numerous murders, and
alongside a team of rogue vampire hunters he must fight Dracula.

17
01:23:38,399 --> 01:23:44,399
Blade: Trinity was released in the United States on December 8, 2004.

18
01:28:33,599 --> 01:28:39,599
The film grossed $132 million at the box office worldwide on a budget of $65 million and received mostly negative reviews
from critics for its formulaic themes, directing, and acting; it is the worst-reviewed film in the trilogy.

19
01:33:28,800 --> 01:33:34,800
The film was followed by a television series, Blade: The Series,
in 2006, with Sticky Fingaz replacing Snipes.

20
01:38:24,000 --> 01:38:30,000
Marvel regained the film rights to the character in 2012.

21
01:43:19,199 --> 01:43:25,199
Snipes reprised his role as Blade in the 2024 film Deadpool &
Wolverine, which starred Reynolds as Deadpool.

22
01:48:14,399 --> 01:48:20,399
A reboot film set in the Marvel Cinematic Universe and starring
Mahershala Ali has been in development since 2019.

23
01:53:09,599 --> 01:53:15,599
The film explores themes of martial arts, loss of
loved one, vampire, fbi, superhero.

24
01:58:04,799 --> 01:58:10,799
The tone is dark and thought_provoking.
